    <string name="fork_01_title">A royal fork</string>
    <string name="fork_02_title">The other corner</string>
    <string name="fork_03_title">A rook in reach</string>
    <string name="fork_04_title">Black\'s royal fork</string>
    <string name="pin_01_title">The pinned defender</string>
    <string name="pin_02_title">A file that matters</string>
    <string name="pin_03_title">Follow the diagonal</string>
    <string name="pin_04_title">Black uses the pin</string>
    <string name="mate_01_title">Deflect the defender</string>
    <string name="mate_02_title">The mirrored finish</string>
    <string name="mate_03_title">Black\'s back-rank net</string>
    <string name="mate_04_title">The left-wing finish</string>
    <string name="fork_01_explanation">Nf7 checks the king on h8 and attacks the queen on d8. After the king moves, the knight wins the queen.</string>
    <string name="fork_02_explanation">Nc7 checks the king on a8 while attacking e8. The king\'s retreat leaves the queen available to the knight.</string>
    <string name="fork_03_explanation">Nf6 attacks the king on g8 and the rook on d7. Answering the check cannot save the rook in this position.</string>
    <string name="fork_04_explanation">Nf2 checks the king on h1 and attacks the queen on d1. The same fork pattern works with Black.</string>
    <string name="pin_01_explanation">The knight on e7 cannot capture the bishop on d5: moving it exposes its king on e8 to the rook on e1.</string>
    <string name="pin_02_explanation">The rook on d1 pins the knight on d7 to its king on d8, so the knight cannot recapture on e5.</string>
    <string name="pin_03_explanation">The bishop on b5 pins the knight on c6 to the king on e8. Qxe5 wins the queen with check; Nxe5 would expose the king.</string>
    <string name="pin_04_explanation">The bishop on b4 pins the knight on c3 to the king on e1. Black can capture on e4 with check because the knight cannot move.</string>
    <string name="mate_01_explanation">Qxf8 forces the king to capture on f8. Rc8 mates: the rook controls the eighth rank, the bishop on g5 covers e7, and the pawns occupy f7 and g7.</string>
    <string name="mate_02_explanation">Qxc8 forces Kxc8. Rf8 mates across the rank; the bishop on b5 covers d7 while the pawns block b7 and c7.</string>
    <string name="mate_03_explanation">Qxf1 forces Kxf1. Rc1 mates along the first rank; the bishop on g4 covers e2 while White\'s pawns block f2 and g2.</string>
    <string name="mate_04_explanation">Qxc1 forces Kxc1. Rf1 mates along the first rank; the bishop on b4 covers d2 while White\'s pawns block b2 and c2.</string>
